Original commit body from 5c5c6e05d0dde6a1d697c47748d5c0ae6c8ea2f5:

Both propagators emitted one TaintFlowFinding per (source call site, sink call
site) pair reachable in the call graph, and each such record asserts "primitive
P1 reached primitive P2". For a flow the ADR-0017 3a walk adjudicated
(analysis_method == "ddg") that claim is earned. For every other flow inclusion
rested on call-graph reachability alone, so n x m records assert n x m data
dependences the walk established none of.

Censused over six repos first: 359 reported flows describing 78 situations
(4.60x), 78% of rows restating a situation already reported, caddy's cmdRun
alone emitting 76. TWO multipliers where the item named one -- 2.87x the
source/sink product inside a symbol, and 1.60x distinct call-graph ROUTES to
the same primitive pair, which are distinct rows only because the consumer's
flow identity keys on `path`, a field documented as one witness route rather
than the route set. So the grouping key names NEITHER primitive; a pair-keyed
fix would have left the second standing.

An unadjudicated finding is now collapsed to one per (taint_label,
source_symbol, sink_zone, sanitized, source_boundary, analysis_method),
carrying source_primitives / sink_primitives / sink_symbols as
module-qualified sets: "symbol S reads {P..Pn} and reaches zone Z via
{Q..Qm}". Qualified because `Do` is not checkable against a catalogue and
`net/http.Client.Do` is (clause a1).

Two departures from the item's own proposal, both priced before taking them:

* ADJUDICATED FLOWS PASS THROUGH. `ddg` confirmed a reaching-def chain from
  the variable the source defines to a use at the sink call site -- that IS a
  pair claim, and it is 6 of the 359 census flows (1.7%).
* `sanitized` and `source_boundary` are IN the key. A sanitized flow is
  excluded from the violation set, so a mixed group would have to be counted
  both ways; and WI-vazal split net_recv / ipc_recv / db_read inside the one
  untrusted_input label precisely so "a request body reached the database"
  stays separable from "a row read from the database reached the database".
  Their presence is what makes collapsing BEFORE the consumer's filters sound:
  every filter verify_taint_claim applies -- label, zone, sanitized, and
  _source_scope's production test, which reads source_symbol and nothing else
  -- tests a field in this key, so no group can be half-included. Asserted by
  a test rather than left as reasoning.

A/B on findings in BOTH signs before shipping, per the INV-nizom precedent.
Arms differing only in this change, same six repos, same claims file, per-arm
XDG_CACHE_HOME, arm A a detached worktree at the parent commit asserted to
LACK the collapse before any measurement. Evidence completeness asserted first
(evidence_count == len(evidence) on every verdict in both arms), so the
coverage check ran over the whole population.

    caddy 219->23  sops 39->11  poetry 13->5
    mitmproxy 60->26  knex 25->12  express 3->3
    TOTAL 359 -> 80 (4.49x)
    VERDICT MOVES: 0.  ARM-A PAIRS MISSING FROM ARM B: 0.

80 rather than the census's 78 because this key is FINER than the census's
(source_symbol, claim); the extra two are boundary/method splits, so 4.49x is
conservative against 4.60x rather than in conflict with it.

The pair count is disclosed, not traded away: `details` gains a "spanning N
source->sink pair(s)" clause (silent when it equals the situation count, so a
single-pair verdict stays byte-identical) and every evidence row carries
collapsed_flow_count. The total is computed over all violations rather than
summed across the capped evidence list, where the sum would be wrong.

Envelope 2.0 -> 2.1: not purely additive, on the 1.5 precedent. The witness
scalars keep their names and stay valid (each is a member of its own set).

One stale reader found. test_cfg.py's _MockTaintFinding hand-restated nine of
the dataclass's fields and raised AttributeError the moment it gained
sink_symbols; it now constructs the real dataclass. cfg.select_ddg_targets
read the witness sink_symbol and now reads the set -- honest scope: that
function has NO production caller today, so this is a latent reader corrected,
not an observed regression.

This makes the CLAIM honest; it does not make the analysis precise. Clause
(a2) remains unmet for every unadjudicated flow, and removal is unsound on
this substrate -- the call graph emits one edge per (caller, callee), so an
edge's `line` is *a* line and not every line.

